    4. operator_fatigue — staffing flexibility vs. fatigue cap interaction
       Q: If the optimiser reduces total labor-hours consumed (shrinking the resource denominator to improve the KPI ratio), can it also reduce operator headcount mid-shift, and if so, is the fatigue bound (≤0.4) applied per individual operator or as a shift-average across all operators?
       A: Headcount is treated as fixed for the shift; the fatigue bound of ≤0.4 is applied to each individual operator independently (worst-case, not average), and the optimizer may only adjust task pacing and sequencing, not staffing levels.
    5. ambient_noise_level — instantaneous vs. time-averaged measurement
       Q: Is the 80 dB hard constraint enforced as a continuous time-averaged LAeq over the whole shift, or as a maximum instantaneous level at any point — since a burst-scheduling strategy that groups noisy operations could satisfy an LAeq limit while exposing operators to prolonged peaks above 80 dB?
       A: The 80 dB limit is enforced as a rolling 15-minute LAeq measured at the operator station, never to be exceeded at any 15-minute window during the shift; instantaneous peaks above 85 dB(A) additionally trigger an immediate corrective action regardless of the rolling average.

