       Q: The priority_order list contains 'Throughput' three times instead of ranking the three actual contract KPIs (resource_efficiency, operator_fatigue, noise_level) — which KPI should be treated as primary, secondary, and tertiary when the optimiser must make trade-offs?
       A: Default priority: resource_efficiency (primary) > operator_fatigue (secondary) > noise_level (tertiary), given that noise_level is already enforced as an inviolable hard constraint and adds no additional optimisation pressure.
    2. resource_efficiency.threshold
       Q: Resource efficiency has no upper bound (threshold: null): if the optimiser can raise the value/resource ratio by ~40% by running machines at maximum speed or eliminating buffer stock, is that acceptable, or should energy draw or machine utilisation be capped (e.g. ≤ 90% of rated machine load)?
