    - Option 2 (Conditional): Temporary Constraint Relaxation with Mandatory Compensating Controls: Request a time-bounded governance waiver to relax FatigueIndex to 0.50 (from 0.40) and Noise to 82.0 dB (from 80.0 dB) for the duration of the elevated-demand window only. Compensating controls are mandatory: (a) enforce 15-minute mandatory rest breaks every 90 minutes per worker to partially offset fatigue accumulation; (b) require PPE hearing protection rated at ≥3 dB NRR for all floor personnel during the waiver period; (c) schedule audiometric checks and fatigue self-assessments daily. Waiver must be logged, time-limited, and reviewed before renewal. This option meets the full demand target with minimal schedule disruption but requires explicit manager sign-off and carries residual worker-health risk.
      Preserves human constraints: No
