    - Option 1 — Workforce Augmentation via Parallel Shift (Recommended): Introduce a second production shift or bring in certified temporary workers to distribute the incremental 25% demand load across additional personnel. By spreading workload over more workers and hours, per-worker fatigue accumulation and sustained noise exposure both remain within policy limits. This approach requires coordination with HR and may incur a 3–5% schedule delay for crew onboarding and safety briefing, but fully preserves all human-centric constraints without any policy waivers.
